# Lunicle — local OAuth credentials.
#
# Copy to `.env` (which is gitignored) and fill in. The dev scripts source it;
# nothing else reads it. Production doesn't use this file at all — Railway holds
# the same four names as service Variables.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Where these come from: docs/oauth-instructions.html. Short version —
#
#   Google   one client covers both production and localhost, because Google
#            allows several JavaScript origins per client. So these two values
#            are the same ones Railway has.
#
#   GitHub   an OAuth app has exactly one callback URL, so local development
#            needs its OWN app ("Lunicle (dev)", callback
#            http://localhost:8080/auth/github/callback). These two values are
#            therefore NOT the ones in Railway, and pasting the production app's
#            credentials here will fail with a redirect_uri mismatch.
#
# Leave a provider blank to disable it locally; the server logs which ones are
# live at startup. Setting only one of a pair is a misconfiguration and the
# server will say so and disable that provider.

GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# From the "Lunicle (dev)" GitHub app — not the production one.
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
